  "fixture_kind": "public_exact-list_card_data",
  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "If an attacking creature loses haste, perhaps because Fervor leaves the battlefield after attackers have been declared, it won't be removed from combat.",
      "oracle_id": "8e0cea9c-3110-4728-9378-76849e33bb90",
      "published_at": "2012-07-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the creature this Aura would enchant is an illegal target by the time Rancor tries to resolve, the Aura spell doesn't resolve. It won't enter the battlefield, so it won't be put into a graveyard from the battlefield and its ability won't trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "9d2d6479-531c-4ce1-b52b-00e36fa63b64",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When the card returns to the battlefield, it will be a new object with no connection to the card that was exiled. Auras attached to the exiled creature will be put into their owners' graveyards. Any Equipment will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled creature will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "a3ec6b5d-08ec-4ae0-b1db-c4b87a1849c7",
      "published_at": "2022-12-08",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "An activated ability has a \"Cost: Effect\" format. Look for the colon. A triggered ability starts with \"when\", \"whenever\", or \"at\".",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It can target delayed triggered abilities. For example, a card that says \"Whenever a player cycles a card, you may exile target creature. If you do, return that creature to the battlefield at the beginning of the end step.\" triggers when a player cycles a card and creates a delayed trigger that happens at the beginning of the end step. You can choose to target the \"at the beginning of the end step\" trigger when it is placed on the stack at end of turn.",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Turn-based actions and special actions like the normal card draw, combat damage, or turning a face-down creature face up can't be targeted.",
      "oracle_id": "b3b00911-ece7-4484-bc36-f211ce72b6cc",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "b685757b-521e-4353-a233-97052359723d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "If the opponent dealt damage controls no planeswalkers, Questing Beast's last ability simply does nothing."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "b685757b-521e-4353-a233-97052359723d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Once a creature with power 3 or greater has blocked this creature, changing the power of the blocking creature won't cause this creature to become unblocked."
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "b685757b-521e-4353-a233-97052359723d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "Questing Beast only stops combat damage from being prevented by effects that specifically use the word “prevent.”"
    },
    {
      "oracle_id": "b685757b-521e-4353-a233-97052359723d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc",
      "comment": "The damage Questing Beast deals to the target planeswalker as its last ability resolves isn't combat damage."
    },
    {
      "comment": "Combat damage dealt by blocking creatures isn’t prevented.",
      "oracle_id": "bfcc3a16-1ca8-4112-a10e-d4e52d3daa8d",
      "published_at": "2010-06-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although Terrifying Presence doesn’t affect the target creature, if that creature is an illegal target when Terrifying Presence tries to resolve, it won’t resolve and none of its effects will happen. No damage will be prevented.",
      "oracle_id": "ca8f6e19-6ef3-4d77-8312-867767ffeda6",
      "published_at": "2012-05-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Spells and abilities that replace or redirect damage are not affected by this card.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The \"damage can't be prevented\" statement overrides all forms of preventing damage. Damage prevention spells and abilities can still be cast and activated, they just don't do anything.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2004-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "\"Flashback [cost]\" means \"You may cast this card from your graveyard by paying [cost] rather than paying its mana cost\" and \"If the flashback cost was paid, exile this card instead of putting it anywhere else any time it would leave the stack.\"",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "A spell cast using flashback will always be exiled afterward, whether it resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a card with flashback is put into your graveyard during your turn, you can cast it if it's legal to do so before any other player can take any actions.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "To determine the total cost of a spell, start with the mana cost or alternative cost (such as a flashback cost) you're paying, add any cost increases, then apply any cost reductions. The mana value of the spell is determined only by its mana cost, no matter what the total cost to cast the spell was.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can cast a spell using flashback even if it was somehow put into your graveyard without having been cast.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must still follow any timing restrictions and permissions, including those based on the card's type. For instance, you can cast a sorcery using flashback only when you could normally cast a sorcery.",
      "oracle_id": "cad19ad2-3ea9-43f5-bb5a-b0793402fab0",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The damage prevention shield lasts for the rest of the turn, and you gain life each time that shield prevents 1 or more damage.",
      "oracle_id": "e245a736-5f65-4159-8e39-e279e1f8794f",
      "published_at": "2005-10-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Because convoke isn't an alternative cost, it can be used in conjunction with alternative costs.",
      "oracle_id": "e245a736-5f65-4159-8e39-e279e1f8794f",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a creature you control has a mana ability with {T} in the cost, activating that ability while casting a spell with convoke will result in the creature being tapped before you pay the spell's costs. You won't be able to tap it again for convoke. Similarly, if you sacrifice a creature to activate a mana ability while casting a spell with convoke, that creature won't be on the battlefield when you pay the spell's costs, so you won't be able to tap it for convoke.",
      "oracle_id": "e245a736-5f65-4159-8e39-e279e1f8794f",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tapping a multicolored creature using convoke will pay for {1} or one mana of your choice of any of that creature's colors.",
      "oracle_id": "e245a736-5f65-4159-8e39-e279e1f8794f",
      "published_at": "2024-01-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Tapping an untapped creature that's attacking or blocking to convoke a spell won't cause that creature to stop attacking or blocking.",
